      article.main
        h1 Comments
        p
          | Buffered comments look the same as single-line JavaScript comments. They act sort of like markup tags, producing
          em HTML
          | comments in the rendered page.
        p Like tags, buffered comments must appear on their own line.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="0")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="1605404495")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  // just some paragraphs
                  p foo
                  p bar
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <!-- just some paragraphs-->
                  <p>foo</p>
                  <p>bar</p>
        p
          | Pug also supports unbuffered comments. Simply add a hyphen (
          code -
          | ) to the start of the comment.
        p
          | These are only for commenting on the Pug code itself, and
          em do not
          | appear in the rendered HTML.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="1")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="-612204649")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  //- will not output within markup
                  p foo
                  p bar
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <p>foo</p>
                  <p>bar</p>
        h2#block-comments
          | Block Comments
          a.header-anchor(href="#block-comments", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p Block comments work, too:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="2")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="1971303801")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  body
                    //-
                      Comments for your template writers.
                      Use as much text as you want.
                    //
                      Comments for your HTML readers.
                      Use as much text as you want.
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <body>
                    <!--Comments for your HTML readers.
                  Use as much text as you want.-->
                  </body>
        h2#conditional-comments
          | Conditional Comments
          a.header-anchor(href="#conditional-comments", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p Pug does not have any special syntax for conditional comments. (Conditional comments are a peculiar method of adding fallback markup for old versions of Internet Explorer.)
        p
          | However, since all lines beginning with
          code <
          | are treated as
          a(href="plain-text.html") plain text
          | , normal HTML-style conditional comments work just fine.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="3")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="-1482941674")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  doctype html
                  
                  <!--[if IE 8]>
                  <html lang="en" class="lt-ie9">
                  <![endif]-->
                  <!--[if gt IE 8]><!-->
                  <html lang="en">
                  <!--<![endif]-->
                  
                  body
                    p Supporting old web browsers is a pain.
                  
                  </html>
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <!DOCTYPE html>
                  <!--[if IE 8]>
                  <html lang="en" class="lt-ie9">
                  <![endif]-->
                  <!--[if gt IE 8]><!-->
                  <html lang="en">
                  <!--<![endif]-->
                  
                  <body>
                    <p>Supporting old web browsers is a pain.</p>
                  </body>
                  
                  </html>
        div(style="margin-top: 50px")
